        a               sh:NodeShape ;
        sh:description  "2: The actsOnCropStage property indicates that the crop management operation acts on a crop that is in a certain crop stage. Crop stages can be:\n1: germination;\n2: leaf development;\n3: formation of side shoots;\n4: stem elongation;\n5: vegetative plant parts;\n6: inflorescence emergence;\n7: flowering;\n8: fruit development;\n9: ripening;\n10: senescence." , "1: This is the class of crop management operations in which the crop/plant is being treated to enhance the performance, e.g. a crop protection operation or pruning operation" ;
